{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.BilinearForm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.KSWallCrossing.primitive_wall_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.KSWallCrossing.primitive_wall_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L117-L117","doc":"**The KS axiom**: for any wall `W` and central charges `Z₊, Z₋` on\nopposite sides, the ordered quantum dilogarithm products are equal.\nThe precise content of \"equal\" depends on the quantum torus algebra;\nwe axiomatize the INVARIANCE of the multiplicity function under\nprimitive wall-crossing (where only `γ₁, γ₂, γ₁+γ₂` contribute). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.KSWallCrossing.spectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.KSWallCrossing.spectrum","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L111-L111","doc":"The BPS spectrum as a function of a central charge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.KSWallCrossing.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.KSWallCrossing.mk","kind":"ctor","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.KSWallCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.KSWallCrossing","kind":"class","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L99-L121","doc":"**Wall-crossing invariance (statement, the KS theorem).**\nGiven two central charges `Z₊, Z₋` on opposite sides of a wall `W`,\nthe ordered products of quantum dilogarithms on each side satisfy\nthe factored relation:\n\n`∏_{arg Z₊(γ) ↗} E(γ)^{Ω₊(γ)} = ∏_{arg Z₋(γ) ↗} E(γ)^{Ω₋(γ)}`\n\nThis is the content of the KS wall-crossing formula. We state it as\nan axiom on the BPS spectra: the spectra on the two sides of the wall\nare related by the KS transformation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.Wall.nonparallel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.Wall.nonparallel","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L97-L97","doc":"The charges are linearly independent (genuine wall, not a fake one). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.Wall.γ₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.Wall.γ₂","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.Wall.γ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.Wall.γ₁","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L94-L94","doc":"The two charges that become aligned. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.Wall.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.Wall.mk","kind":"ctor","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.Wall","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.Wall","kind":"structure","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L90-L97","doc":"A **wall** is a codimension-1 locus in the space of stability conditions\nwhere two BPS charges become aligned: `arg Z(γ₁) = arg Z(γ₂)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSSpectrum.states","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSSpectrum.states","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The set of BPS states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSSpectrum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSSpectrum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSSpectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSSpectrum","kind":"structure","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L77-L80","doc":"A **BPS spectrum** is a (finite) collection of BPS states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSState.multiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSState.multiplicity","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The BPS degeneracy / DT invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSState.charge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSState.charge","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The charge of the BPS state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSState.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSState.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.BPSState","kind":"structure","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L69-L75","doc":"A **BPS state** is a charge `γ` with a positive integer multiplicity `Ω(γ)`.\n(The Donaldson-Thomas / BPS invariant.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.CentralCharge.map_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.CentralCharge.map_add","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Additivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.CentralCharge.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.CentralCharge.Z","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The central charge function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.CentralCharge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.CentralCharge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.CentralCharge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.CentralCharge","kind":"structure","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L61-L67","doc":"A **central charge** on a charge lattice: a group homomorphism `Z : Γ → ℂ`.\n(Stated abstractly as a function with additivity.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.euler_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.euler_self","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L53-L57","doc":"Self-pairing vanishes for antisymmetric forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.euler_add_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.euler_add_left","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Bilinearity in the first argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.euler_antisymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.euler_antisymm","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Antisymmetry: `⟨γ, δ⟩ = −⟨δ, γ⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.euler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.euler","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The antisymmetric (Euler) pairing `⟨γ, δ⟩ ∈ ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.addCommGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.addCommGroup","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.Γ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.Γ","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The underlying abelian group (typically `ℤ^n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice.mk","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WallCrossing.ChargeLattice","kind":"structure","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WallCrossing.lean#L38-L49","doc":"A **charge lattice** with an antisymmetric integral pairing.\nThis is the combinatorial data underlying a Bridgeland stability condition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}